;; A yield point in a body-local function that recurses, but not in tail
;; position.
;;
;; The self-recursive half of `errors/suspend_in_mutual_local_functions.bjo`,
;; and the one a reader is most likely to hit: `go` is written the way anyone
;; writes a fold by hand, and the recursive call sits inside a `+`.
;;
;; So it is a call rather than a jump, `go` has to be a real function for its
;; own name to refer to, and it stays a C# local function — which is the one
;; body-local shape that still cannot suspend.
;;
;; The `while` fix is the accumulator: `158_local_functions.bjo`'s `countdown`
;; is this function made tail recursive, and it compiles and suspends. The
;; second fix is lifting `go` to a top-level `(defbjo ...)`, which also works —
;; a top-level bjoroutine may recurse however it likes, because it is a method
;; and an await is legal anywhere in one.
;;
;; Both are named in the message, because only one of them applies to every
;; case that reaches it: a genuine value use cannot be made tail.

;; EXPECT-ERROR: calling 'fetch' is a yield point
;; EXPECT-ERROR: 'go' is a loop, but it still mentions its own name
;; EXPECT-ERROR: make every mention of 'go' a tail call
;; EXPECT-ERROR: lift it out to a top-level (defbjo ...)

(: fetch (-> int int))
(defbjo (fetch x) (* x 2))

(: outer (-> int int))
(defbjo (outer n)
  (defun (go i)
    (if (<= i 0)
        0
        (+ (fetch i) (go (- i 1)))))
  (go n))

(defun (main args) 0)
